    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75489" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρχήστ-ρα</span></b> , ἡ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ʽὀρχέομαἰ</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>orchestra,</i> i.e. in the
			theatre the <i>space on which the chorus danced,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				901b30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				577.31
			</span></i> (Milet., <span class="entity">iii/ii B. C.</span>), etc.: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. πολέμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.193e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>part of the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγορά</span> at Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				26e
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Tim.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i></div>
